  "notes": {
    "006B60": "The player's health ($FFFE62, max $FFFE60, in apples) changes by d0 here: negative for a hit, positive when healed. player_health_change() scales the hits by the difficulty and drops them with infinite health; 100% keeps the original.",
    "006268": "Widescreen: the scroll's column draw ($624A) takes its column from the camera's plus d6 (0 moving left, 22 moving right); ws_col() moves it out by ws_cols blocks. A column left of the camera's is the same plane column as one 32 to the right, so d6 keeps the game's own wrap working.",
    "01892C": "Widescreen: the field camera ($188D2) clamps its left edge to [$FFA4FA, $FFA4FC]; these four instructions use ws_cam_lo()/ws_cam_hi(), the limits brought in by the extra width.",
    "00781A": "Widescreen: 18 places check whether an object is near the screen (x + bias - camera against a limit) before updating or drawing it. Each subtracts camera - ws_extra and compares against limit + 2 ws_extra, so objects in the side areas live and show."
  }
